# Line endings are policy, not luck.
#
# This repository is authored on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, which has so
# far normalised everything to LF on the way into the index. That is a property
# of one contributor's git configuration, not of the repository: anyone with
# core.autocrlf=false — the default on Linux and macOS — who edits a shell
# script commits CRLF, and `sh` then reads the carriage return as part of the
# command. `.husky/pre-commit` fails as `lint-staged\r: not found`, a Dockerfile
# RUN line breaks the image build, and nginx rejects its own configuration.
# Each of those reports a problem that looks nothing like a line ending.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Files an interpreter reads directly, where a stray \r is a syntax error
# rather than a cosmetic difference.
.husky/*        text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.mjs           text eol=lf
*.cjs           text eol=lf
Dockerfile      text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*    text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf

# Generated: reformatting a lockfile makes `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`
# fail, so it is committed exactly as pnpm writes it.
pnpm-lock.yaml  text eol=lf -diff

# Binary — never translate, never diff.
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.ico           binary
*.ttf           binary
*.otf           binary
*.woff          binary
*.woff2         binary
*.pdf           binary
